 :context
 "ISIC Rev.5 1399 (Manufacture of other textiles n.e.c.) had no prior
  actor implementation -- gh api confirmed
  repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1399 returned 404 before this
  work started. The registry's live {:id \"1399\" :name \"Manufacture
  of other textiles n.e.c.\" :maturity :spec ...} entry was verified
  against a fresh clone (via a targeted grep of the git-cloned
  registry.edn blob, not the CDN-cached raw.githubusercontent.com
  mirror) before any work began, confirming no ID/name mismatch. 1399
  is a residual n.e.c. textile category (nonwovens, felt, tire-cord
  fabric, other technical/industrial textiles) distinct from siblings
  1392/1393/1394. Fresh, from-scratch scaffold, built as part of a
  smaller, carefully verified batch (capable model + mandatory
  verification) after an earlier 18-agent haiku batch's 61% defect
  rate; 138+ consecutive agents on this stricter protocol had
  succeeded prior to this one. Module shape mirrors sibling
  cloud-itonami-isic-1394 (Manufacture of cordage, rope, twine and
  netting)'s verified module shape -- the closest domain analog
  (physical-safety-relevant plant equipment, production-batch
  tracking, permanent equipment-control block) -- domain-adapted for
  nonwoven/felt fabric manufacturing (this build's own chosen concrete
  illustration for the residual 1399 class), substituting
  area-square-meters for length-meters and adding a TWELFTH governor
  check for basis-weight-gsm (basis-weight-test plausibility) alongside
  a renamed tensile-strength-kn check (in place of 1394's single
  breaking-strength-kn), both explicit domain requirements named in
  the task spec."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Coordination-only actor. Closed four-op allowlist, all :effect
   :propose: log-production-batch, schedule-maintenance,
   flag-safety-concern (always escalates), coordinate-shipment. An op
   outside this set is a HARD hold (unknown-op-violations)."
  :governor-rules
  "Twelve HARD, permanent, un-overridable checks elaborating four
   blueprint invariants: (1) plant/batch record must be independently
   verified/registered before any action -- equipment-not-verified
   (schedule-maintenance) / batch-not-verified (coordinate-shipment) /
   shipment-area-exceeded (independently recomputed against the
   batch's own logged area-square-meters, never the proposal's own
   claim); (2) request :effect must be :propose only
   (not-propose-effect, evaluated first, unconditional); (3) any
   proposal touching forming/bonding-line-equipment control is a hard,
   permanent block -- equipment-control-blocked (closed proposal-
   :effect allowlist) AND line-operate-blocked (:direct-operate? true
   on a maintenance proposal), two independent layers, neither ever a
   member of any phase's :auto set; (4) closed op-allowlist
   (unknown-op). Plus already-scheduled (double-schedule guard),
   invalid-grade, invalid-tensile-strength (> 0, <= 500.0 kN),
   invalid-basis-weight (this build's own second domain-specific
   addition -- must be a strictly positive, physically plausible gsm
   reading, > 0 and <= 5000.0), invalid-defect-rate. Soft confidence/
   high-stakes gate: flag-safety-concern always escalates regardless
   of confidence (high-stakes set + nonwovenops.phase's permanent
   absence of this op from every phase's :auto set -- two independent
   layers agree); low confidence (<0.6) also escalates. Only
   log-production-batch may auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when
   governor-clean."
  :module-shape
  "nonwovenops.store (MemStore, batches + equipment directories seeded
   with a verified/registered batch with shipping headroom, a
   verified/registered batch nearly fully shipped, and an UNVERIFIED
   batch; one verified/registered forming-line unit and one
   UNVERIFIED bonding-line unit), advisor (NonwovenAdvisor, mock +
   real-LLM seam via langchain.model), governor (Nonwoven & Technical
   Textiles Plant Operations Governor), phase (0->3 rollout), operation
   (langgraph-clj StateGraph via langgraph.graph, interrupt-before
   #{:request-approval}), sim (demo driver exercising all three
   happy-path escalate/approve flows plus all twelve HARD-hold
   scenarios directly)."}
